    {
      "id": 99764,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-04-20T13:42:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"j1hopki1\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/58f4c7/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> j1hopki1:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Does anyone know how long a game of Sentinels Tactics takes? Is it the same as Sentinels of the Multiverse, which is usually an hour, or is it a lot longer?&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Don't know! I have played five times. I have yet to play a game that didn't have at least one person who was learning the game for the first time.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>PLUS, beyond learning the game itself, learning the abilities of the various characters becomes important. Take a bunch of people who know the game but not the characters they are playing and the game will slow down.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:27:50.673Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
