    {
      "id": 99772,
      "name": "Silverleaf",
      "username": "Silverleaf",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-04-22T01:04:39.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"grim88\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/c77e96/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> grim88:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If you hire rooms do you rent people? Crazy Brits and their messed up bastardization of the English language…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>We say \"rent\" when we mean a kind of permanent-ish arrangement. You'd rent a house (or a room in a shared house) to live in, or rent a storage unit to store your collection of old orange skins and stuffed otters and out-of-date tubes of hemarroid cream in.</p>\n<p>You'd hire a room for a few hours, or hire a floor sander for the weekend, or hire a boat for the day.</p>\n<p>You totally&nbsp;<em>can</em> rent people, but it's usually on a very temporary basis, and you probably wouldn't want to tell your significant other about it. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
      "post_number": 11,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:27:51.280Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
