      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"grim88\"]\n\nIf you hire rooms do you rent people? Crazy Brits and their messed up bastardization of the English language... \n[/quote]\n \n\nWe say &quot;rent&quot; when we mean a kind of permanent-ish arrangement. You&#39;d rent a house (or a room in a shared house) to live in, or rent a storage unit to store your collection of old orange skins and stuffed otters and out-of-date tubes of hemarroid cream in.\n\nYou&#39;d hire a room for a few hours, or hire a floor sander for the weekend, or hire a boat for the day.\n\nYou totally&nbsp;<em>can</em> rent people, but it&#39;s usually on a very temporary basis, and you probably wouldn&#39;t want to tell your significant other about it. ;)\n",
